.\" kzero(1) - declarative Kubernetes workload pipelines
.\" Manual page for kzero
.TH KZERO 1 "2026-06-29" "kzero v0.8.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
kzero \- declarative Kubernetes workload shutdown and startup pipelines
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B kzero
.I command
[\fIoptions\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B kzero
is a Go CLI that runs ordered
.B down
,
.B up
, and
.B reset
pipelines from a YAML profile. Operators scale Deployments and StatefulSets,
run Helm release helper scripts or the in-process Helm SDK, and invoke custom
shell steps with phase and per-step hooks. Configuration is validated before
cluster mutations; use
.B analyze
and
.B run.mode: dry-run
to review plans first.
.PP
With
.BR run.execution:
.BR native
or
.BR auto ,
workload and
.B release.*
steps use the Kubernetes and Helm Go clients when possible; host
.BR kubectl
and
.BR helm
are optional on that path.
.PP
During live
.BR down ,
.BR up ,
and
.B reset ,
optional
.B run.api_watchdog
monitors API reachability and can cancel a stalled step after
.BR fail_after .
.PP
kzero is not self-contained: hooks and
.B custom:
steps run
.BR /bin/sh ;
some profiles still require host
.BR kubectl
and
.BR helm .
Install them when your YAML expects shell-based release scripts or kubectl
subprocesses.
.PP
Operator deployment patterns (bastion, cron, kind e2e): see
.IR https://github.com/hrodrig/kzero-selfhosted .
Full schema:
.IR https://github.com/hrodrig/kzero/blob/main/SPECIFICATIONS.md .
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B analyze
Validate config and print a normalized execution plan (no cluster mutations).
.TP
.B target
Print the Kubernetes target block (context, cluster, kubeconfig path).
Use
.B --output slug
for a sanitized cluster name only (wrapper log filenames).
.TP
.B notify test
POST to enabled
.B notify.*
channels without running a pipeline.
Use
.B --event
to preview
.BR pipeline.start ,
.BR pipeline.success ,
.BR pipeline.error ,
.BR pipeline.stalled ,
or
.BR notify.test .
.TP
.B verify
Run post-up readiness checks (
.B workloads_ready
,
.BR nodes_ready ,
.BR pods_schedulable ).
.TP
.B probe
Run the optional
.B infra_probe
mini-pipeline (registry, PVC, Helm checks).
.TP
.B down
Run
.B hooks.pre-down
, then
.B pipelines.down
, then
.B hooks.post-down
(fail-fast).
.TP
.B up
Run
.B hooks.pre-up
, then
.B pipelines.up
, then
.B hooks.post-up
.
.TP
.B reset
Run full
.B down
then
.B up
; if
.B down
fails,
.B up
does not run. Re-runs API preflight between phases.
.TP
.B version
Print version, commit, build date, and branch.
.SH OPTIONS
Global flags apply to all commands:
.TP
.BR \-c " , " \-\-config " \fIpath\fR"
Config file path. Default when omitted:
.IR ./kzero.yaml .
After a Linux package install, use
.IR /etc/kzero/kzero.yaml
or copy the sample to the working directory.
.TP
.BR \-\-print\-sample\-config
Write the sample profile to stdout and exit (same as
.IR configs/kzero.sample.yml ).
.TP
.BR \-\-log\-format " \fItext|json\fR"
Structured logging for pipeline commands (default
.BR text ).
.TP
.BR \-\-log\-level " \fIdebug|info|warn|error\fR"
Minimum log level for text output (default
.BR info ).
.TP
.BR \-\-no\-env\-passthrough
Omit host environment from hook and subprocess env (only
.BR KZERO_*
and
.BR KUBECONFIG ).
.SH ENVIRONMENT
Variables with prefix
.B KZERO_
override YAML when loaded (see SPEC). Examples:
.BR KZERO_RUN_MODE ,
.BR KZERO_RUN_KUBECONFIG ,
.BR KZERO_COMMAND_KUBECTL ,
.BR KZERO_COMMAND_HELM .
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ./kzero.yaml
Default config in the current working directory.
.TP
.I /etc/kzero/kzero.yaml
Example profile installed by Linux
.BR .deb /
.BR .rpm
packages (
.B config|noreplace
on upgrade).
.TP
.I share/examples/kzero/kzero.sample.yml
Sample profile inside release tarballs.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Print sample config:
.RS
kzero \-\-print\-sample\-config > ./kzero.yaml
.RE
.TP
Validate and print plan:
.RS
kzero analyze \-\-config ./kzero.yaml
.RE
.TP
Dry-run shutdown pipeline:
.RS
kzero down \-\-config ./kzero.yaml
.RE
.TP
Live reset (after review):
.RS
export KZERO_RUN_MODE=live
kzero reset \-\-config ./kzero.yaml
.RE
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success; non-zero on config validation errors, hook failures, or pipeline step failures.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR kubectl (1),
.BR helm (1)
.PP
Project: https://github.com/hrodrig/kzero
